Bad mental habits." "Okay, teach me." You know, he says, "Okay."

00:24:47.120 --> 00:24:49.400
DANG PO NYON MONGS PA SKYER BCUG

00:24:50.120 --> 00:24:57.880
Let's say you have a problem with anger towards somebody like someone has been upsetting you. Okay, So you're not angry. You're not throwing,

00:24:59.120 --> 00:25:01.240
you're not throwing things all day.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:04.360
I had recently a couple call me and they said we're

00:25:04.360 --> 00:25:05.400
at the throwing stage.

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:07.440
We're starting to throw things at each other

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:10.520
I said, okay, we have to, we have to
cover this second husband thing.

00:25:11.120 --> 00:25:12.760
Okay

00:25:12.760 --> 00:25:14.760
DANG PO NYON MONGS PA SKYER BCUG

00:25:15.560 --> 00:25:17.560
So when you're sitting by yourself

00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:21.000
and you're calm and

00:25:21.760 --> 00:25:24.720
you know, you're kind of mildly happy,

00:25:25.560 --> 00:25:28.400
if you're at the throwing stage with your partner,

00:25:28.400 --> 00:25:30.480
you know, tossing things at each other,

00:25:32.200 --> 00:25:34.120
They weren't throwing things at each

00:25:34.160 --> 00:25:35.560
other, they were throwing garbage cans

00:25:35.560 --> 00:25:36.320
on the floor and stuff.

00:25:37.760 --> 00:25:41.080
So anyway, NYON MONGS PA SKYER BCUG

00:25:41.400 --> 00:25:46.680
Close your eyes and try to recreate the situation.

00:25:46.680 --> 00:25:49.120
So close your eyes and

00:25:49.920 --> 00:25:52.080
this person comes into your room and

00:25:52.760 --> 00:26:00.080
they start saying something which really, really hurts you. Really hurts your heart, you know, and try to recreate

00:26:00.840 --> 00:26:04.720
this situation while you're calm and you're sitting on the couch and

00:26:05.080 --> 00:26:12.080
close your eyes and imagine your husband comes in and starts accusing you of something or something like that.

00:26:12.080 --> 00:26:14.880
Just do that. SKYER BCUG means

00:26:15.560 --> 00:26:17.760
see if you can get to that emotion

00:26:18.760 --> 00:26:20.080
artificially.

00:26:20.080 --> 00:26:26.040
See if you can get yourself upset just thinking about your husband. That's kind of a funny,

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.880
it's an amazing trick. Okay?

00:26:28.880 --> 00:26:31.160
DE NAS NYON MONGS

00:26:32.040 --> 00:26:37.480
Then you'll get upset, you know, you'll feel upset, then open your eyes real quick

00:26:38.120 --> 00:26:44.600
and try to catch how it feels to be upset. Okay?
Like try to catch the feeling.

00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:45.800
NGOS ZIN

00:26:45.800 --> 00:26:52.400
NGOS ZIN means learn to recognize how it feels to start to get upset

00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:59.720
by practicing getting upset, by thinking about the bad things your husband said to you in the past.

00:27:00.080 --> 00:27:07.000
It's very amazing method, you know. We should have put it in the meditations Tim, maybe you guys can do it in the groups

00:27:08.640 --> 00:27:10.640
Get used to identifying

00:27:11.360 --> 00:27:13.360
how it feels to start to get upset

00:27:14.160 --> 00:27:16.920
in your own heart. Okay,

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:21.280
by doing upset meditations. That's so cool.

00:27:23.080 --> 00:27:25.800
SKYER BCUG GNYEN PO BSTEN

00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:29.120
And then practice applying the antidote.

00:27:29.400 --> 00:27:32.520
"Oh, oh he's not coming from his side. He's coming

00:27:32.520 --> 00:27:35.600
from me. When he says those things to me

00:27:36.120 --> 00:27:38.680
that's coming from me.

00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:41.400
I have to remembered that, I have to remember,"

00:27:42.920 --> 00:27:45.120
YENGS NA'ANG NGOS ZIN PA'I GNAD YOD

00:27:45.120 --> 00:27:46.440
Then he makes a funny,

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:51.920
he says, he's so funny. He says,
"Look it's going to mess up your whole day.

00:27:52.640 --> 00:27:56.320
YENGS NA'ANG means it's going to mess up your whole day.

00:27:56.320 --> 00:27:58.040
NGOS ZIN PA'I GNAD

00:27:58.040 --> 00:28:01.120
This is the marma, what do you it call it? Marma hata.

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:05.720
The killing point, but there's a GNAD, GNAD here means,

00:28:07.080 --> 00:28:12.400
yeah, it's gonna throw your whole day off balance

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:13.600
to do this meditation where you practice getting upset

00:28:13.600 --> 00:28:14.400
at your husband, but

00:28:15.400 --> 00:28:17.000
NGOS ZIN PA'I GNAD

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:21.640
the crucial point of this mini meditation is to

00:28:21.800 --> 00:28:23.800
learn to identify

00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:27.080
how it feels to be upset, so when you start

00:28:27.080 --> 00:28:29.040
to get upset you can stop yourself.

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:31.720
YOD TSUL SOGS GSUNGS,

00:28:31.920 --> 00:28:34.440
That's how our teacher wrapped up

00:28:34.440 --> 00:28:36.600
the morning's comments.

00:28:36.960 --> 00:28:39.560
And that's how we're wrapping up this episode.

00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:45.240
So thank you for coming to Lam Rim.
Don't forget to practice this upset meditation,

00:28:45.280 --> 00:28:49.680
if you're lucky your husband will just come in the room and help you and

00:28:50.680 --> 00:28:54.320
you know, it actually works pretty well.
By the way, we're not trying to identify

00:28:55.960 --> 00:29:02.440
what it feels like to be upset, we all know that, okay. We're trying to learn to recognize

00:29:06.120 --> 00:29:08.120
What it feels to start to get upset.

00:29:08.600 --> 00:29:12.280
Because that's where you can stop it. Once you're upset. It's almost impossible to stop.

00:29:13.040 --> 00:29:15.040
So, if we could learn to recognize

00:29:16.240 --> 00:29:20.760
the first few minutes of being upset,
then we could do something about it.

